{title: Surrounded by Songs}
{subtitle: Psalms 32:7–8}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] |
| [F] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Day and [Dm]night [Gm]your hand was heavy
My vigor [Eb]turned [Bb]to summer dryness
I [Dm]made my sin known [Eb]to you
[F]I did not [Bb]cover up my guilt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are my [Dm]hiding place
You guard me from [Gm]all trouble
Sur[Eb]round me with songs
Songs of [Bb]deliverance
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I will in[Dm]struct [Gm]you and teach
The way you [Eb]should [Bb]go is clear
I will coun[Dm]sel you and [Eb]watch
O[F]ver you [Bb]with tender care
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are my hiding [Dm]place
You guard me from all trou[Gm]ble
Surround me [Eb]with songs
Songs of deliverance
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Dm] | [Eb] | [F] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Do not be like a [Dm]horse
Without [Eb]understanding or sense [Bb][F/A]
[Gm]Bit and bridle only [Dm]curb
Else it [Eb]will not come [Fsus4]near
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Many sorrows mark the wic[Dm]ked
[Gm]But trust in the Lord is [Eb]love
[Bb]Steadfast love surrounds the [Dm]soul
Who [Eb]leans up[Fsus4]on his [Bb]grace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are my hiding place
You guard [Dm]me from all trouble
Surround [Gm]me with songs
Songs [Eb]of deliverance
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [Dm] | [Eb] | [Fsus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Rejoice in the Lord be glad [Dm]
[Eb]Shout for [Fsus4]joy in heart
{end_of_verse}

